# UPGRADE-14

# Fully Self-Hosted Local AI Stack

# Local Model Gateway, Real Runtime Verification,

# Hardware-Aware Routing, Local Embeddings/RAG,

# MCP 2026-07-28, Benchmarking,

# and Zero-Cost Autonomous Coding Pipeline

You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-13.

PRIMARY PRINCIPLE:

NO-COST FIRST.

The objective is to prove that a useful autonomous coding workflow can
run from beginning to end without:

* Anthropic API key
* OpenAI API key
* paid LLM API
* Stripe
* hosted vector database
* hosted embeddings
* paid MCP infrastructure
* paid observability
* Redis
* Kafka
* cloud object storage
* cloud KMS
* commercial analytics

External providers remain OPTIONAL adapters.

================================================================
MISSION
=======

Build and verify a genuinely self-hosted AI execution layer:

ZCoder
│
├── Local Model Gateway
│     ├── Ollama
│     ├── vLLM
│     ├── OpenAI-compatible local servers
│     └── future local engines through adapters
│
├── Hardware Profiler
│     ├── CPU
│     ├── RAM
│     ├── GPU
│     └── VRAM
│
├── Model Discovery
├── Capability Registry
├── Model Router
├── Benchmark Engine
│
├── Local Embeddings
├── Local RAG / Repository Index
│
├── MCP Registry
│     ├── local stdio
│     └── HTTP MCP
│
└── Autonomous Coding Runtime
│
├── inspect
├── plan
├── edit
├── test
├── review
└── validate

The highest-level acceptance scenario is:

fresh machine
→ install ZCoder
→ detect local AI backend
→ discover model
→ benchmark capabilities
→ index repository locally
→ execute coding task
→ use tools
→ modify isolated worktree
→ run tests
→ validate result
→ store artifacts locally
→ zero paid API calls

