16. GPU DETECTION
=================

Detect only installed hardware/runtime.

Potential vendors:

NVIDIA
AMD
Apple
CPU-only

Do not install drivers automatically.

================================================================
17. NVIDIA
==========

Use safe local mechanisms where available.

Examples:

nvidia-smi

Do not require CUDA Python library just for detection.

================================================================
18. AMD
=======

Detect ROCm-capable environment where actually available.

Do not classify every AMD GPU as ROCm-compatible.

================================================================
19. APPLE
=========

Detect Apple Silicon architecture.

Do not claim CUDA/ROCm semantics.

================================================================
20. CPU-ONLY MODE
=================

CPU must remain a supported profile.

Do not fail startup because no GPU exists.

Recommend smaller/quantized models.

================================================================
21. MEMORY SAFETY
=================

Model recommendation must account for:

RAM
VRAM
quantization
context

Do not start a model known to exceed configured safety threshold.

================================================================
22. RESOURCE POLICY
===================

Allow:

max_ram_percent
max_vram_percent
max_cpu_threads

Avoid exhausting developer machine.

